  "title": "Erdős Problem #942",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $h(n)$ count the number of powerful (if $p\\mid m$ then $p^2\\mid m$) integers in $[n^2,(n+1)^2)$. Estimate $h(n)$. In particular is there some constant $c>0$ such that $ h(n) < (\\log n)^{c+o(1)} $ and, for infinitely many $n$, $ h(n) >(\\log n)^{c-o(1)}? $ ",
